  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a lead from Sarah Tan in the Analytics Department. The project kicked off on June 15th with an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One, which was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. The executive board subsequently approved a total budget of $2M covering all research, development, and marketing phases, with a specific $55,000 allocated for the compliance plan. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. The project has established strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI research and is leveraging AI to enhance data visualization tools. A detailed progress report will be shared in a staff meeting on November 20th."
